@               Configuration Editor (Bus Editor SubMenu)
               -----------------------------------------

Use this editor  to modify the bus configuration information.

Field Description:
------------------
1. Bus Request Priority:
                     This gives the bus request priority level. 0 - 3
                     correspond to BR0 - BR3.
2. Fair Requester Timeout:
                     This gives the delay time for Fair Requester in
                     microseconds. Valid values are 2 to 28 in increments
                     of 2. Value of 0 means that Fair requesting is
                     disabled.
3. Bus Release Mechanism:
                     The options are Release on Request (0) or Release
                     on Done (1).
4. Bus Arbitration:
                     The options are Priority (0) or Round Robin (1).
5. Local Bus Timeout:
                     This gives the timeout time for the local bus. The
                     valid options are 4 to 512 microseconds in powers
                     of 2. A value of 0 means that local bus timeout is
                     disabled.
6. VXI Bus Timeout:
                     This gives the timeout time for the VXI bus. The
                     valid options are 4 to 512 microseconds in powers
                     of 2. Select 0 to disable VXI bus timeout if the
                     VXIcpu-030 is not the system controller.
6. VIC Port:
                     Bit 0 set selects the VIC as a 32-bit port. Bit 0 clear
                     selects the VIC as a 16-bit port.

Usage
-----
It supports the following commands:

(1) list      [<index#>,[<index#>]] - lists all the entries in the 
                                          specified range.
(2) display   [<index#>,[<index#>]] - displays the entries in detail.
(3) modify    <index#>              - lets you modify an existing entry.
(4) save                            - lets you save the information.
(5) abort                           - lets you exit the editor,
                                      ignoring the changes made.
(6) exit                            - lets you exit the editor.
(7) help                            - gives help on that editor.
@


